1165:| OD50 | <a id="od50"></a>Reserved or contextual `from` and `until` (added 2026-10-29, from the reviews of OD47). Options: (a) reserved words everywhere, as OD47 first said: `let from: Int` is refused and the lexer has two more keywords; (b) contextual keywords, meaningful only between `for IDENT` and the block, so existing names stay legal. Recommendation: (a), one lexical rule and no context-dependent tokens, at the cost of two names; Austral reserves its loop words Reviewed pick (2026-10-30, a recommendation that supersedes the recommendation above where they differ): (a) reserved everywhere | the current compiler has neither word (bug 331) | bug 331's repair; SYN-1 | decided 2026-10-31 by the owner's rule (every reviewer agreed, as strict as Austral or stricter): Reserved everywhere |
